  "equipment_type": "Air handling / make-up air unit controller (BMS command points)",
  "applies_to": "Engineered Air appliances (air handlers, make-up air, indirect and direct gas-fired heaters, DX and energy recovery units) built with the CenCon controller, version 3.0.0 or later.",
  "summary": "CenCon is Engineered Air's unit controller, with BACnet MS/TP (19200 or 38400 baud), BACnet IP and Modbus RTU. It works as a virtual BACnet gateway, and CenCon_SW (device Gateway ID + 55) is the software device that holds every writable EMS point: the fan start enable, module enables, dehumidification, reheat, pre-cool and economizer overrides, the discharge, DX, humidity and damper setpoints and the XP_XM spare outputs. It also reports the heating, cooling, humidification, recovery, dehumidification, reheat and pre-cool demands.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "CenCon version 3.0.0 or higher",
  "default_device_instance": "Gateway ID + 55 (default Gateway ID 270000, so 270055)",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "CenCon_SW is always present. The sensors, relays and expansion-module I/O are on the CenCon and module devices (separate library entry).",
    "Temperatures are integers in tenths of a degree F (780 = 78.0 °F); write setpoints the same way.",
    "Points depend on unit type and arrangement; enables for modules that are not fitted do nothing.",
    "The table marks the writable points R/W; the manual says writes use priority 3 to 7, so they are shown as commandable.",
    "Source: CenCon_SW tables on pages 8-9 of IOM65 R106 (50 objects)."
  ],
  "source": {
